  <prompt>Add an OBO-identity assertion to every user-scoped grounded tool description so no flow ever asks the user for their identity (the P2 dead-end). The assertion states that the tool "returns the calling user's own records over OBO; never ask the user for their identity." Apply it to `GridOverviewHandler.Metadata.Description` AND its byte-equal JSON seed row (`infra/dataverse/sprk_analysistool-grid-overview-row.json`) keeping the two byte-equal (the D-4 parity test enforces byte-equality against the handler Metadata.Description), AND to the other user-scoped tools (grep for OBO / user-scoped handlers). Re-seed and verify the D-4 parity test stays green.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. .NET 8 Minimal API + AI tool-catalog expertise; comfortable with the Services/Ai grounded-tool handlers, the byte-equal seed-row convention, and the D-4 parity test that guards handler-description ⇄ seed-row equality.</role>
  <goal>Every user-scoped tool description asserts "returns the calling user's own records over OBO; never ask the user for their identity", so a prioritize/today flow never asks for the user's id or name — with the GridOverviewHandler description and its byte-equal seed row kept byte-equal (D-4 parity green).</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-05 / QW1 — the OBO-identity wording quick win. User-scoped grounded tools already read the caller's own records over OBO (ADR-028), but their descriptions do not tell the model this, so the model can ask the user "what is your id/name?" — a dead-end (P2). The fix is pure description wording: assert the OBO identity contract in each user-scoped tool's description. `GridOverviewHandler` (the My-Tasks grid overview tool) carries a `Metadata.Description` that MUST stay byte-equal with its JSON seed row `infra/dataverse/sprk_analysistool-grid-overview-row.json` — the D-4 parity test guards this byte-for-byte, so the same assertion string MUST be added identically to both. Other user-scoped handlers (e.g. DailyBriefingOverviewHandler and any other OBO user-scoped tool) get the same assertion; grep the Services/Ai handlers for OBO / user-scoped tools to find the full set. This is a description/data change only — no query logic, no dispatch change. redesign-r2 is CLOSED so Services/Ai is R4-editable; keep AI-facade discipline (ADR-013) and /conflict-check for shared-file overlap with compose-r5/r6 + assistant-r3.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/GridOverviewHandler.cs (Metadata.Description — add the OBO-identity assertion; keep byte-equal with the seed row)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/sprk_analysistool-grid-overview-row.json (the byte-equal seed row guarded by the D-4 parity test — add the identical assertion string)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/DailyBriefingOverviewHandler.cs (+ its seed row, if present — another user-scoped OBO tool to apply the assertion to)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/ (grep for OBO / user-scoped handlers to find the complete set of user-scoped tool descriptions)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (the D-4 parity test guarding handler-description ⇄ seed-row byte-equality)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project" scope="the tool descriptions">Add the OBO-identity assertion ("returns the calling user's own records over OBO; never ask the user for their identity") to every user-scoped tool description; MUST NOT change query logic or dispatch — description/data only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="GridOverviewHandler description ⇄ seed row">Keep the C# `Metadata.Description` byte-equal with the JSON seed row — the D-4 parity test enforces byte-for-byte equality; add the identical assertion string to both and re-seed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013" scope="Services/Ai placement">Preserve the Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ facade discipline; do NOT inject AI-internal types into CRUD code even though Services/Ai is now R4-editable (redesign-r2 closed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF §10" scope="every BFF-touching change">Publish size ≤60 MB compressed (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs) — measure and report absolute + delta; no new HIGH CVE from `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/spec.md</file>
