    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Identify the full set of user-scoped grounded tools: read GridOverviewHandler + DailyBriefingOverviewHandler and grep the Services/Ai handlers for OBO / user-scoped (caller's own records) tools.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the OBO-identity assertion string to each user-scoped handler's `Metadata.Description`.</step>
    <step order="3">For GridOverviewHandler (and any handler with a byte-equal seed row), add the identical assertion string to the JSON seed row `infra/dataverse/sprk_analysistool-grid-overview-row.json` so it stays byte-equal with the handler description.</step>
    <step order="4">Re-seed the affected rows.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the D-4 parity test and confirm it is green (byte-equality preserved).</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build + dotnet publish size check; record absolute size + delta; run the vulnerable-package scan.</step>
    <step order="7">/conflict-check before the PR; update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <justification>
    <existing>User-scoped tool descriptions (GridOverviewHandler, DailyBriefingOverviewHandler) already exist; they read over OBO but the description does not assert the identity contract.</existing>
    <extension>Amend the existing descriptions (+ byte-equal seed rows) with one assertion sentence — no new surface, description/data only.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The model asks the user for their id/name on today/prioritize flows (the P2 dead-end); OBO already knows the identity, so the ask is a defect.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/GridOverviewHandler.cs (Metadata.Description with the OBO-identity assertion)</output>
    <output type="code">infra/dataverse/sprk_analysistool-grid-overview-row.json (byte-equal seed row with the identical assertion)</output>
    <output type="code">the other user-scoped tool descriptions (+ any byte-equal seed rows) carrying the assertion</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The OBO-identity assertion is present in `GridOverviewHandler.Metadata.Description`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The identical assertion is present in the byte-equal seed row and the D-4 parity test is green (byte-equality preserved).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The assertion is applied to the other user-scoped tool descriptions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A prioritize/today flow never asks for the user's id or name (manual UAT) — negative case.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size ≤60 MB reported (absolute + delta).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Description/data change only — do NOT touch query logic or the pre-filter. The D-4 parity test is the guard: the handler `Metadata.Description` and its seed row MUST stay byte-for-byte equal, so add the exact same assertion string to both. redesign-r2 is closed (Services/Ai R4-editable) but keep AI-facade discipline; /conflict-check with compose-r5/r6 + assistant-r3 before the PR.</notes>
